; ============================================================
; TITLE:    City at Night
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     random, skyline, FILLED, windows, stars, layers
; SUMMARY:  Builds a random city skyline at night with lit windows, stars and a full moon.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Buildings of random width and height stand shoulder to shoulder
;   across the screen. Each has a grid of windows, and each window
;   is lit (yellow) or dark at random. Behind the city, stars and a
;   big moon shine in a deep blue sky.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run for a new city every time.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * WHILE to keep adding buildings until the street is full
;   * nested FOR loops for rows and columns of windows
;   * keeping shapes side by side so they never overlap
;   * a chance with RANDOM: lit if (random 10) < 6
;   * remembering roofs in a list so stars only appear in the sky
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make more windows dark, as if it is very late.
;   * Give some buildings a pointed roof or an antenna.
;   * Draw a second row of shorter, darker buildings in front.
; ============================================================

; BUILDING paints one building from x to x + w, h tall, standing on
; the street at y = -260, then fills it with windows.
to building :x :w :h
  penup setxy :x -260 setheading 0
  filled pick [[30 30 50] [40 35 60] [25 40 55] [45 45 65]] [
    repeat 2 [forward :h right 90 forward :w right 90]
  ]
  windows :x :w :h
end

; WINDOWS draws rows and columns of small square windows. A window
; is a short thick line, so it is painted on top of the building.
to windows :x :w :h
  setpensize 7
  for [wy -240 -270 + :h 20] [
    for [wx :x + 10 :x + :w - 10 14] [
      ifelse (random 10) < 6 [setpencolor [255 220 120]] [setpencolor [55 55 80]]
      penup setxy :wx :wy pendown
      setheading 0 forward 4
    ]
  ]
end

; SKYLINE keeps adding buildings left to right until it reaches the
; right side of the screen. It remembers each roof as [left right top]
; so the stars can stay out of the buildings later.
to skyline
  localmake "x -400
  while [:x < 400] [
    localmake "w (random 50 110)
    localmake "h (random 90 360)
    building :x :w :h
    make "roofs fput (list :x :x + :w -260 + :h) :roofs
    make "x :x + :w + (random 0 6)
  ]
end

; ROOF.AT outputs the height of the roof above x, or the street level
; if x falls in a gap between buildings.
to roof.at :x
  foreach :roofs [
    if and :x >= item 1 ? :x <= item 2 ? [output item 3 ?]
  ]
  output -260
end

; NIGHT.SKY scatters stars, but only where there is sky, then hangs
; up a moon high above the tallest building.
to night.sky
  repeat 300 [
    localmake "x (random -400 400)
    localmake "y (random -150 300)
    if :y > 6 + roof.at :x [
      setpencolor pick [[255 255 255] [200 200 255] [255 240 200]]
      setpensize (random 1 3)
      dot list :x :y
    ]
  ]
  setpencolor [250 245 220]
  setpensize 90
  dot [270 210]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [12 18 50]
make "roofs []
skyline
night.sky
; the street
penup setxy -400 -280 setheading 90 pendown
setpencolor [20 20 25] setpensize 40
forward 800
